<p>President Trump on Monday refused to apologize for his public criticism of Pope Leo XIV, saying &quot;there&#x27;s nothing to apologise for&quot; and that the pope is &quot;wrong on the issues,&quot; after the pontiff criticized the war in Iran. Trump escalated the dispute by calling Leo &quot;WEAK on Crime&quot; and &quot;terrible for Foreign Policy,&quot; turning it into an unusually public clash between the White House and the Vatican. The standoff shows no sign of easing. In the latest development, Pope Leo said he had &quot;no fear of the Trump administration&quot; and would keep speaking out against war.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/t1COQI7ELKXRgQqSI1Z3zcByEO4WvTt75m7TUHVAeMDHWVVVN1b5GUf3pUTry0rIeDwhEHC3DSlogRWnwCR0jqhCsBXag8gLwlvUeeT05ypOp4WcNXKLMmNnGpeecOaHH752X1vgC32gmW7RvMIdDE8L9e7BDwzxNyWg--3aKZe9Hp6hyGplXd1uGy0SWj-8xg9TdyH-2GAQmtNjkN2T1CjlyVofdpEaoXpXbn6O0dOrqQNjk2Lx3SjHrdK9uRGOwQb9EwxXaDrqvJPAFw' alt='Pope Leo XIV leaves after presiding over a Prayer Vigil and Rosary for Peace, in Saint Peter&#x27;s Basilica at the Vatican, April 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Fact check: PBS reported that Trump&#x27;s claim that Pope Leo supports Iran getting a nuclear weapon is contradicted by the pope&#x27;s own statements opposing nuclear weapons and warning of their devastation.</li><li>Catholic reaction: NDTV and The Globe and Mail reported that the confrontation unsettled many U.S. Catholics across ideological lines, leaving even some voters generally sympathetic to Trump uncomfortable.</li><li>Deleted post: PBS reported that Trump also tried to explain away a now-deleted social media post depicting him as Jesus, saying he thought the image showed him as a doctor.</li><li>Election risk: The Straits Times said the feud could hurt Trump politically by alienating parts of the religious right ahead of November&#x27;s U.S. midterm elections.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo XIV: Leo warned that violence was becoming normalized and that religious language could be misused to justify war, framing his intervention as a moral warning rather than a personal feud. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/pope-leo-says-no-fear-trump-administration-lashes-out/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump said Leo should stop &quot;catering to the radical left,&quot; casting the dispute as both ideological and strategic. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/13/donald-trump-pope-leo'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Giorgia Meloni: Meloni&#x27;s rebuke stood out because it came from a prime minister widely seen as a close Trump ally. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cp841y07w5xo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>U.S. Catholics: Some faithful Trump supporters said the president crossed a red line by attacking the pope directly, even though they were otherwise sympathetic to him. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-in-feud-with-the-pope-trump-crosses-red-lines-for-some-faithful/'>The Globe and Mail</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-iran-war-hes-wrong-very-weak-on-crime-trump-refuses-to-apologise-to-pope-leo-11353133#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;He&#x27;s Very Weak On Crime&quot;: Trump Refuses To Apologise To Pope Leo</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cp841y07w5xo'>Italian PM condemns ally Trump over &#x27;unacceptable&#x27; Pope criticism</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/13/donald-trump-pope-leo'>I do not fear Trump, says Pope Leo after US president calls him ‘weak’</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/pope-leo-says-no-fear-trump-administration-lashes-out/'>Pope says he has &quot;no fear of the Trump administration&quot; after president lashes out</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/us-politics/article-trump-opens-a-new-front-in-his-war-on-everyone-the-vatican/'>Trump opens a new fron